!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/link/valid/a-refined-constructor-applied-is-its-own-kind-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/link-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.3 (construction sugar, proposed for Revision 40), [TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §8.2"
  description: """
    `nonempty_type` refines `meta.array`, pinning `min_items`, so it is a constructor, and construction sugar
    applies it over its one remaining required field typed by a reference naming types: `nonempty_type<uuid>` is
    `!nonempty_type { element_type: uuid }`. That is an instance of `nonempty_type`, its own kind, and a different
    entry from `[uuid; 1..]`, which is `!meta.array { element_type: uuid  min_items: 1 }`: the two admit the same
    data and neither is rewritten to the other. So the kind over `nonempty_type` admits the first and not the
    second.
    """
  valid: {
    binds: [nonempty_type_uuid_xxhash array_uuid_1_xxhash]
    members: [
      { name: nonempties  members: [nonempty_type_uuid_xxhash] }
    ]
  }
}
